??  The Wikipedia had a simple coefficient in the regression:

   beta_raw * x[n]

If we change the model to include the term

    beta * (1 - lambda) * x[n]

then

    beta = beta_raw / (1 - lambda).

And so if beta_raw > 0, then as lambda -> 1, we have
beta -> +infinity.

Or am I totally missing something here?  (Wouldn't be
the first time!)

