To all who are following along in the quest for koyck model estimation to allow for rho to be near 1, attached is an earlier version of adl_gibbs.pdf that provides al ofl the gory details as far as  what happens to
the posterior of (lambda,beta) density as lambda approaches 1. If one sits down with pencil and paper, it actually ends up making sense because the posterior derivation involves only integration and a lot of algebra. The paper also explains a fix for the problem so I plan to use exactly their priors along with the fix in STAN and see what happens as rho goes near 1.0. I will also try Ben's earlier recommendation. If either of the latter work, then I will go back to JAGS and see if the same fix works there also. It would be more interesting of course if STAN succeeded and JAGS didn't but we shall see.

                                                                                                                                                                                                                    Mark

