Thanks, Jiqiang.  I was sure I had done as you described, but I had missed the part about removing the older version when rstan is not loaded.  I verified that by noticing that the installation process couldn't copy the new rstan.dll into place; I still had the 1.2.0 version.  I quit all R ESS sessions and started over, and now it works.

It's probably obvious to everyone else, but it wouldn't hurt to add that comment to https://code.google.com/p/stan/wiki/RStanGettingStarted.

Bill

